<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ carrier text arrives at the shore; normalize bytes (strip a leading BOM, fold CR into LF).
⏿ orient: does an SOH sentinel frame a carrier? `MemeStreamParser` scans for carrier-open/close events across single-meme, multi-meme, and partial input.
◇ decide: each carrier-close routes through `splitMemeToTiddlers`; a bare doc (no SOH framing) falls through to a verbatim-body split.
▶ split ahu slots recursively into child tiddlers, rewrite each block to a `<<~ kahea ahu #/slot>>` reference in the parent, and grade the parse via `parseMemeText().failures`.
↺ verify: a split failure degrades loss-lessly (verbatim fallback, `lar_parse_degraded`), warnings ride a `parse-warning` tiddler that `deserializeCarrier` reads into `MemeDiagnostic[]` — text-in, records-out, no `fs`/`path`/`window`. Callers own persistence and routing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

`deserializeCarrier(text, fields)` gates all carrier ingress, returning `{ records: TiddlerFields[]; diagnostics: MemeDiagnostic[] }`. It delegates the split to `memeticWikitextDeserializer` (the TW5 `tiddlerdeserializer` export) and lifts synthesised parse-warning tiddlers onto the shared diagnostics contract, so a caller reads a grade rather than sniffing a title. Isomorphic — no `fs`, no `path`, no `window`; the host passes text, the shore returns typed records.

The shore marks the causal-island boundary (spec: TW5 VM). `memeticWikitextDeserializer` uses `parseMemeText` and `MemeStreamParser` (both TW5-independent) to fold one carrier into a parent tiddler plus N ahu-slot children. Decomposition law begins here: non-TW5 adaptation stops at this shore.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/source>>

!! Source (TypeScript — compiled to a tiddlerdeserializer plugin tiddler)

```typescript
export function deserializeCarrier(
  text:   string,
  fields: Record<string, unknown>,
): { records: TiddlerFields[]; diagnostics: MemeDiagnostic[] } {
  const records = memeticWikitextDeserializer(text, fields);
  const diagnostics: MemeDiagnostic[] = [];
  for (const record of records) {
    if (!String(record.title ?? "").includes("/parse-warning/")) continue;
    for (const line of String(record.text ?? "").split("\n")) {
      if (line.trim()) diagnostics.push(shoreDiagnostic(line.trim(), text.length));
    }
  }
  return { records, diagnostics };
}
```

